From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] verilated_runtime: do not link -latomic on Linux

The same zero-sysroot problem as the verilator module's own patch, one
level up: verilated_runtime adds -latomic on Linux, and every simulator
built by verilator_cc_library depends on it, so the flag lands on the
final link of each generated simulator rather than only on verilator
itself.

The BCR "llvm" toolchain (hermetic-llvm) ships no libatomic -- its
runtime is compiler-rt -- so the link fails with

    ld.lld: error: unable to find library -latomic

libatomic is GCC's out-of-line fallback for atomics the hardware cannot
do inline. The verilated runtime uses atomics on types clang lowers
inline on x86-64 and aarch64, so nothing here needs the library; on a
toolchain that does ship it, dropping the flag costs an unused -l.

Not upstreamed: the correct upstream fix selects on the C++ runtime
rather than on the OS, which is a change to make in rules_verilator on
its own terms. Retire this patch at a release that makes -latomic
conditional.
---
 verilator/BUILD.bazel | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/verilator/BUILD.bazel b/verilator/BUILD.bazel
--- a/verilator/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/verilator/BUILD.bazel
@@ -32,10 +32,7 @@
 
 cc_library(
     name = "verilated_runtime",
-    linkopts = select({
-        ":linux": ["-latomic"],
-        "//conditions:default": [],
-    }),
+    linkopts = [],
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
     deps = ["@verilator//:verilated"],
 )
